NOTES.update({
424:'Marjolin Femme d’Alatri et de Frosinone CSR AG254 is one 24.5×19.5 cm graphite/pen/black-ink sheet with two portraits, hair/jewelry studies and a detailed necklace clasp. The inscribed regional names identify the combined study; constituent motifs do not multiply its count.',
425:'Ary Renan Etude de femmes 93.1.9 is the 20.2×11.2 cm pen/black-ink drawing on tracing paper, marked AR. The native description offers several uncertain mythological readings; retain uncertainty rather than choose Apollo/Daphne or Eve. One sheet counts once.',
426:'George Sand Paysage D89.9.1 is the 16×24 cm dendritic watercolor of a rocky valley against misty mountains, with separate frame and 1953 bequest. It differs from the landscape with two figures and dog 2002.6 in described composition. Generic anonymous oil landscapes are different media; no exact year follows from technique history.',
427:'Portrait présumé du Duc d’Orléans CSR AG14 is the 33.2×28.2 cm pastel/charcoal drawing attributed to Ary Scheffer, with illegible signature and red-pencil 1834. Keep both presumed sitter and attributed maker, retaining the source broad date. Scheffer’s Chantilly PE446 is a 64×43 cm oil canvas; Henry Scheffer is a different maker.',
428:'Anonymous Paysage marin CSR AG48 is the 12.7×21.4 cm watercolor with fishermen/boat silhouettes and a dominant sky. Exact-title comparisons are larger oil paintings or a 1965 tempera by other named makers; these physical forms differ from this nineteenth-century paper watercolor.',
429:'Marjolin Etude de coiffure CSR AG256 is the 9.5×6.9 cm graphite drawing of a complex bun with hairpin, with frosinone inscribed at upper left. CSR AG251’s braid study has the inscription at upper right and another format; preserve these physical distinctions rather than rely only on inventory.',
430:'Ary Renan Deux personnages enlacés 93.1.8 is the 22.3×13.1 cm pen/black-ink drawing on tracing paper, marked AR. The possible Pygmalion/Galatea interpretation remains tentative. Gustave Moreau’s Des8082 has a different supplied maker; no title-only merge is made.',
431:'Etude de cavalier CSR AG15 is the 31×37.7 cm watercolor/graphite study attributed to Ary Scheffer, with written uniform-color notes and Scheffer-Renan collection annotation. Preserve the attribution; the related duke’s entry is a subject/model relationship, not an asserted identical finished work.',
432:'Anonymous Deux femmes dans un intérieur CSR AG33 is the 31.2×23.5 cm watercolor/graphite/brown-ink drawing with circled verso 9. One woman kneels beside the other; the related same-title work requires within-batch comparison. Existing Cornélia Marjolin-Scheffer depicts a woman with two children, a different described subject.',
433:'Marjolin CSR AG258 is one 11.2×16.7 cm graphite sheet with two female-costume studies and a wicker basket. These are motifs on one study sheet, not three records; broad nineteenth-century dating remains.',
434:'Ary Renan 93.1.10 is the 17.3×25 cm pen/black-ink study sheet, marked AR, with Latin costume/pose annotations. The described folio is treated as one catalogue unit with separate mount; individual antiquarian studies are not counted separately.',
435:'Lénore ou le retour de l’armée CSR AG16 is the 31.6×53.4 cm watercolor attributed to Ary Scheffer, titled on the reverse, with separate mount and frame. Preserve explicit native attribution and broad nineteenth-century date. Future and past exhibition entries do not establish current display.',
436:'Anonymous Casimir Dudevant D92.2 is the 23×16.3 cm graphite portrait, with Carnavalet stamp and reverse note describing a 1928 auction purchase. Native 1992 reassignment explains historical custody; the purchase is not the drawing’s production year.',
437:'Marjolin CSR AG259 is the 11.1×8.4 cm graphite sheet containing a woman carrying a head load and a braided-bun portrait. Its combined two motifs differ from isolated hairstyle sheets; count one physical drawing.',
438:'Ary Renan 93.1.12 is the 22.5×13.7 cm graphite drawing on tracing paper, monogrammed AR, of a partly undressed woman carrying a load on her right shoulder. It differs from Marjolin’s small head-load and hairstyle sheet by maker, support and composition.',
439:'Ary Scheffer Géricault sur son lit de mort 2001.5 is the 10.3×15.6 cm graphite drawing on laid paper, marked A.S. and 18 January 1824. Preserve that physical inscription even though the narrative says Géricault died on 26 January; the title does not license silently changing the date. The Louvre painting and Vie romantique painted replica are different object forms.'
})
HOLDS.update({
421:'George Sand Paysage de Nohant 2017.6.2 is a 16.2×22.8 cm watercolor with sparse native description, near the sizes of other selected dendritic landscapes. Compare its composition with those notices before treating the different title/accession alone as proof of another physical work.',
422:'Marthe et Marguerite CSR AG13 repeats the exact reverse Copie par un élève ? text of CSR AG34 (388), with different size/medium and attributed rather than model-author Scheffer label. Resolve the related copy/version relationship and possible measurement/catalogue duplication before adding the additional notice.',
440:'Anonymous Vue d’une plage CSR AG40 is a 24×42 cm ink/pen/wash drawing. One exact-title existing lead by Lionel Noël Royer lacks physical details; compare its primary medium/composition before excluding it from an anonymous-source match solely by maker label.'
})
