HOLDS[423]='Anonymous Intérieur d’atelier 95.4.1 is a 29.7×20.6 cm oil on card signed HS. Several exact-title existing records (Tassaert, Van Hecke, Ryckaert, Possoz) lack physical descriptions; compare their primary objects before excluding a possible reattribution/catalogue duplicate. Other leads on canvas/wood or pastel differ materially. Do not expand HS into a guessed artist.'
NOTES.update({
441:'Marjolin Deux femmes auprès d’une fontaine CSR AG246 is the 18.3×13 cm graphite drawing of one woman bathing a child and another carrying a jar. This combined fountain scene differs from his seated mother/child and doorway studies; one sheet counts once.',
442:'Ary Renan Saint Brandan 93.1.15 is the 17.2×14 cm graphite portrait study, marked AR and St Brandan, with separate mount. The saint’s identity is depicted content, not medieval creation; unrelated existing portrait leads have different sitters and makers.',
443:'Anonymous Scène champêtre auprès d’un moulin CSR AG53 is the 51×42.3 cm pencil/pen/ink/wash drawing on laid paper with VDL and figure/sphere/shield watermark. Count this documented sheet once; the near-identical related CSR AG54 notice is held for comparison rather than assumed another work.',
444:'Marjolin Enfant emmailloté CSR AG247 is the 20.4×21 cm graphite drawing with Rome inscription and watermark. The two angles of the swaddled child in its mother’s arms share one described drawing; no two-work count is inferred.',
445:'Ary Renan Femme assise de profil 93.1.18 is the 28.3×22 cm graphite drawing, monogrammed AR, with face turned left. It differs from frontal seated 93.1.6 in pose and sheet dimensions; source nineteenth-century period remains.',
447:'Marjolin Recueil Golfe Juan CSR AG312 is the entire beige 16×24.5 cm sketchbook, marked RM/Golfe Juan/1885 and René Marjolin inside the cover. Count the bound volume as one catalogue artwork, retaining circa 1885 and its annotated landscape-sketch description; no constituent pages are created.',
448:'Ary Renan 93.1.21 is explicitly one double-sided 18×9.5 cm sheet in pen/ink/sanguine/pencil, with two figures leaning on trees and a reverse male-face fragment. Preserve tentative Dryad interpretation and count the physical sheet once.',
449:'Anonymous Scène de bataille CSR AG56 is one 46.5×58.5 cm double-sided graphite/pen/ink/wash drawing: cavalry battle on the front and two rider studies on the back. The two sides and multiple figures are one physical object.',
450:'Marjolin Carnet CSR AG316 is the entire 26.5×36 cm sketchbook of 32 leaves with brown woven cover, signature, Dupin stationer label and a dated 28 February 1874 flower study. Count the bound volume once, retain circa 1874 and full scope, and do not create 32 leaf records or convert the stationer into artist.',
451:'Ary Renan Eude de femme assise 93.1.22.1 is explicitly one 18.8×14.3 cm double-sided graphite drawing, marked AR. The reverse figure has an inverted crescent on her bodice; preserve the title typo and both sides without making two works.',
452:'Anonymous Chiens d’Ernest Renan CSR AG57 is the 29.9×46.7 cm watercolor with literal Ch. Frantz/Pinx signature. Add Frantz to identity comparison without inventing a first name or authority. The resting dog and two hunting dogs share one landscape composition.',
453:'Marjolin Attelage de deux bœufs CSR AG204 is the 21.2×28.5 cm graphite drawing of a yoked pair and protective yoke device. The animals and equipment occupy one study sheet; no precise date or multiple objects are inferred.',
454:'Ary Renan Saint Brandan 93.1.35 is the 27.5×17.5 cm full-length graphite study with bell, anchor and alternate left-arm positions, marked AR and St Brandan. Its full figure/attributes and format differ from the smaller portrait study 93.1.15.'
})
HOLDS.update({
446:'CSR AG54 repeats CSR AG53’s medium, VDL figure/sphere/shield watermark, donor and near-identical 51×42 cm dimensions, with only the added ruins wording. Compare compositions or primary object history before counting the additional notice as a second physical drawing.',
455:'Anonymous Béranger 2004.5 is a 72.5×51 cm engraving with uncertain R. Barbier dedication, but the native subject index names Ary Scheffer and an existing Scheffer Béranger portrait lacks physical detail. Resolve the model/print/identity comparison with primary evidence; do not infer the dedicator as maker or create a second object from title alone.'
})
